{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Final epic evidence and residual-gap disposition before close (merged tree 694cf894def36241724e7049e3308d782037ef6d):\n- All 12 direct children are closed; nested children are closed through their certified parents. The final two coordinated leaves landed as Gerrit 1592 and 1595, each with LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, and no unresolved comments.\n- Canonical surface, compatibility vocabulary/defaults/codes, plain-language flags, durable pause, core push ownership, and corrected dry-run guidance are proven by the recorded core paths plus tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_cli_heldout.py and tests/scripts/test_run_reconcile_bridge_heldout.py.\n- Python library and MCP parity are proven by src/rebar/_lib_ops.py, src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py, and tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_programmatic_heldout.py. Pip, Homebrew wheel, and MCP/uvx installation are proven by tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_runner_install_paths_heldout.py.\n- Local, GitHub Actions, Jenkins, GitLab CI, and bare execution, one shared command/secret/timeout contract, offline GitLab schema validation, and pinned mandatory shellcheck are proven by tests/unit/workflow/test_bridge_provider_wrappers_heldout.py. Full-depth behavior and named shallow-clone rejection are proven by tests/scripts/test_run_reconcile_bridge_heldout.py.\n- Provider-neutral destructive-repair safety and absence of a gh subprocess are proven by src/rebar/_commands/_repair_pause.py and tests/scripts/graph/test_repair_pause_ownership.py.\nResidual-gap sweep: CLI, library, MCP, automated callers, install paths, and legacy/canonical dual-direction compatibility are fixed in scope; no surface slot or planned behavioral test was excluded. The repository architecture remains Python-first: orchestration is packaged Python and the provider files are thin declarative wrappers, with no new repository shell runner. The parent close-gate evidence-discovery issue was fixed by independently measurable criteria and closed with a normal signed PASS, not force or weaker validation. Shared release-note overlap is accepted because the changes landed sequentially without conflict. Remaining compound matrix wording is accepted where one assertion intentionally binds a shared cross-provider invariant. No new ADR is required because existing user, reuse, CLI/MCP, and release docs record the contract; review independently dropped the ADR concern as low-validity."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786431727263255001,"uuid":"0c4543f8-9278-4364-a3c7-540675a5f9fe"}